{"ts": "2026-10-31T14:15:08.731866Z", "run_id": "r-20261031T1409Z-233f", "unit": "openspec:add-admin-cli", "seq": 32, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-001", "id": "Q-001", "status": "answered", "reason": "I read the frozen test: line 82 creates bob with name \"Bob B\", line 160 expects the text line to end in \"Bob\", line 270 expects displayName \"Bob B\". In src/identity/users.ts the display name of a new user is the trimmed name claim (displayValue only cuts at 200 code points), so the stored value is \"Bob B\". The spec and design say the text line's last column is the display name through safeText, which leaves \"Bob B\" unchanged. Only line 160 disagrees with the fixture, the JSON expectation and the stored value, so the clarifier suggestion, which fixes that one line, is the correct minimal change. Option 2 would also be consistent but edits two lines for no reason.", "called": true, "tasks": ["7.4"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.0613285000000001, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "df4c0df73755eae6260ccd24798f3df70338c6fa8e2c4203976a0d6e2c2c13d7", "checked": [{"ref": "src/cli/admin/list-users.test.ts:82", "quote": "upsertUserFromClaims(tx, a, { issuer: ISS, subject: \"bob-sub\", name: \"Bob B\" }, { ids, clock })", "claim": "The fixture creates bob with the name claim \"Bob B\"."}, {"ref": "src/cli/admin/list-users.test.ts:160", "quote": "const bobLine = (bob: User): string => `${bob.userId}\\thuman\\tactive\\t\\t\\tBob`;", "claim": "The text helper expects bob's line to end in \"Bob\", which disagrees with the fixture."}, {"ref": "src/cli/admin/list-users.test.ts:270", "quote": "displayName: \"Bob B\",", "claim": "The JSON scenario in the same file expects bob's display name to be \"Bob B\"."}, {"ref": "src/identity/users.ts:111", "quote": "nameValue ?? displayValue(preferred) ?? displayValue(email) ?? displayValue(subject) ?? subject;", "claim": "A new user's display name is the name claim when present."}, {"ref": "src/identity/users.ts:81", "quote": "const cut = Array.from(value).slice(0, 200).join(\"\").trim();", "claim": "displayValue only cuts at 200 code points and trims, so \"Bob B\" is stored verbatim."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/ops-cli/spec.md#requirement-admin-list-users-shows-the-tenants-users", "quote": "id, kind, state, roles, teams, display name with control characters as `?`", "claim": "The last column of a list-users text line is the display name."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md", "quote": "Line: id, kind, state, roles and teams (each joined by `,`), `safeText(displayName)`, tab-separated", "claim": "The design prints safeText(displayName) as the last column, which leaves \"Bob B\" unchanged."}]}
